1
00:00:01,159 --> 00:00:02,965
Welcome to ACME Clinical,

2
00:00:02,965 --> 00:00:06,434
a central monitoring station for hospital wards.

3
00:00:06,434 --> 00:00:09,116
Staff sign in with their hospital account,

4
00:00:09,116 --> 00:00:11,309
and each role sees its own menu.

5
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:15,156
The ward overview shows every bed at a glance:

6
00:00:15,156 --> 00:00:18,901
twelve fictitious patients and ten simulated monitors,

7
00:00:18,901 --> 00:00:22,379
with vital signs in large, easy-to-read numbers.

8
00:00:24,974 --> 00:00:28,061
Switch to 3D to see the unit in space.

9
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:30,006
Beds light up by alarm state,

10
00:00:30,006 --> 00:00:33,174
and a nurse walks to the most urgent patient.

11
00:00:35,608 --> 00:00:39,728
Live monitoring streams heart rate, oxygen saturation,

12
00:00:39,728 --> 00:00:41,864
respiration, blood pressure,

13
00:00:41,864 --> 00:00:44,608
and a synthetic ECG for every bed.

14
00:00:47,038 --> 00:00:49,874
In the Simulation Lab, we choose a monitor,

15
00:00:49,874 --> 00:00:51,852
apply the low oxygen scenario,

16
00:00:51,852 --> 00:00:54,376
and advance the clock by one minute.

17
00:00:56,801 --> 00:00:58,813
The alarm appears right away.

18
00:00:58,813 --> 00:01:01,169
Acknowledging it records who responded,

19
00:01:01,169 --> 00:01:04,763
but the alarm stays active while the condition continues.

20
00:01:09,301 --> 00:01:13,142
Each patient record brings together trends, alarm history,

21
00:01:13,142 --> 00:01:15,013
and clinical observations.

22
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:20,868
Devices tracks battery, connection, and sensor health,

23
00:01:20,868 --> 00:01:23,649
and biomedical staff log maintenance work.

24
00:01:26,052 --> 00:01:28,416
Alarm limits are set for each unit,

25
00:01:28,416 --> 00:01:30,727
with patient-specific overrides.

26
00:01:33,098 --> 00:01:35,463
Reports are generated in Python,

27
00:01:35,463 --> 00:01:38,273
and can be downloaded as PDF or CSV.

28
00:01:40,618 --> 00:01:45,030
Administrators manage the team, and assign each person's role.

29
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:51,733
Every event is logged and saved, so results survive a reload.

30
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:53,996
That's ACME Clinical.
